build/
.gradle/
.kotlin/
.idea/
*.iml
.DS_Store
_to_delete/

# Local working notes — not part of the published source.
CLAUDE.md

# The wrapper jar MUST be committed — CI runs ./gradlew and cannot bootstrap without it. This
# negation is defensive: a global or ancestor ignore matching *.jar would otherwise drop it
# silently, and the failure would surface on a runner rather than here.
!gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar

# Nothing secret belongs in this repo. Signing identities, notarization credentials and the PGP
# release key all come from the environment (build.gradle.kts) or from CI secrets; these patterns
# are a backstop, not the policy.
local.properties
keystore.properties
*.p12
*.jks
*.keystore

# Release artifacts and CI outputs pulled down for signing — never commit binaries. This is not
# tidiness: a 100+MB artifact committed by accident is rejected by GitHub at push time, and the
# only fix is a history rewrite. The AppDir and appimagetool below are created in the workspace
# by the release workflow and by anyone reproducing it locally.
/ci-artifacts/
/*.AppDir/
/appimagetool-*.AppImage
/squashfs-root/
/PGPony-*.dmg
/PGPony-*.deb
/PGPony-*.msi
/PGPony-*.tar.gz
/PGPony-*.AppImage
/SHA256SUMS
/SHA256SUMS.asc
